WEBVTT

00:14:56.836 --> 00:15:00.236
or how you kind of navigate power,
we can unpack that a little bit.

00:15:00.276 --> 00:15:02.036
Sophia: Yeah, my pleasure, thank you.

00:15:02.076 --> 00:15:04.236
This conversation is, like,
giving me shivers.

00:15:05.076 --> 00:15:08.676
My family and I, we came to the States
when I was five years old.

00:15:08.676 --> 00:15:12.396
And as so many first-generation
immigrants, you know,

00:15:12.436 --> 00:15:18.476
we poured everything into,
kind of embodying that model minority

00:15:18.516 --> 00:15:21.236
and working really hard and assimilating,

00:15:21.236 --> 00:15:25.396
and all to secure some social capital
within a new country, right?

00:15:26.116 --> 00:15:29.596
And then I don't think
it was until my early 30s

00:15:29.636 --> 00:15:33.196
when I started really reaching
some heights in my career.